  "Question": "If \\(78\\) is divided into three parts which are proportional to \\(1,\\) \\(\\dfrac13,\\) \\(\\dfrac16,\\) the middle part is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\dfrac13\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(17\\dfrac13\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\dfrac13\\)",
    "E": "\\(26\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Multiplying all three ratio terms by \\(6\\) preserves their relative sizes and gives\n\\[\n1:\\frac13:\\frac16=6:2:1.\n\\]\nThus the total consists of \\(6+2+1=9\\) equal units, and the middle-sized part contains \\(2\\) of them. Its value is\n\\[\n78\\cdot\\frac29=\\frac{52}{3}=17\\frac13.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(17\\frac13\\), choice C.",
